{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788972997,"nonce":"sQBLBmetKcNHvS6gVDVHT9fo/oM=","title":"Found while implementing `ae84a07`. `ability-cast` refuses any `AbilityDef` with","message":"`targetWorldCell:true` at a named gate (`world-target-unsupported`) rather than\nfaking it, which is the honest answer but is a real capability gap.\n\n\n`RimWorld/Ability.cs` has TWO queue paths and this issue shipped one:\n\n- `QueueCastingJob(LocalTargetInfo target, LocalTargetInfo destination)` —\n  shipped. `JobDefOf.CastAbilityOnThing`, map-local.\n- `QueueCastingJob(GlobalTargetInfo target)` — NOT shipped. Builds\n  `def.jobDef ?? JobDefOf.CastAbilityOnWorldTile` with `job.globalTarget`, and\n  **branches on `pawn.IsCaravanMember()`: a caravan member does not take a job\n  at all, it calls `Activate(target)` directly.**\n\nThe gate chain differs too, and reusing this issue's would be wrong:\n\n- `Ability.CanApplyOn(GlobalTargetInfo)` reads the `EffectComps` PROPERTY, not\n  the private field — so it does NOT have the silent-skip trap the local\n  overload has, and the two must not share an implementation.\n- `Ability.ValidateGlobalTarget(GlobalTargetInfo)` is the target-layer check,\n  and it calls `EffectComps[i].Valid(target, throwMessages: TRUE)` — the true\n  form throws top-of-screen messages, so a verb reproducing it must pass false.\n- `AbilityDef.showGizmoOnWorldView` and `Ability.WorldMapExtraLabel` are the\n  world-view gizmo surface; `Ability.GetGizmos`' clauses are the map ones.\n- `def.targetRequired` is still honoured, but a `GlobalTargetInfo` is a tile,\n  not a cell — `abilities`' target argument (`\"x,z\"`, `[x,z]`, landmark,\n  `pawn:\u003cid\u003e`) has no spelling for one.\n\nRoyalty's own `Skip`-family psycasts are map-local; the world-target shape is\nmostly Royalty's `CallRoyalAid`-adjacent and modded abilities. On a bench with\nno such def this is inert, which is why it is filed rather than built.\n\n\n- `ability-cast` accepts a WORLD TILE target — a new argument spelling\n  (`tile:\u003cplanetTileId\u003e`, distinct from `target`, because a tile id and a\n  thingIDNumber are both bare integers and confusing them casts at the wrong\n  thing silently).\n- It routes through `Ability.QueueCastingJob(GlobalTargetInfo)`'s clauses\n  reproduced, not through the local overload, and **the caravan branch is\n  reported as its own `order_effect`**: `Activate(target)` runs immediately,\n  takes no job, and burns `def.cooldownTicksRange.RandomInRange` on the shared\n  Rand stream, so \"the cast is queued\" is false there and must not be printed.\n- The target-layer check is `ValidateGlobalTarget` reproduced with\n  `throwMessages:false`; a `true` there raises a message per refusing comp.\n- `abilities` publishes `target_world_cell` (it already does) AND, for such a\n  def, a `world_target` block naming the tile forms accepted — a row that says\n  `castable:true` with no way to name a target is the defect this closes.\n- The confirmation pre-check covers the `GlobalTargetInfo` overload of\n  `Ability.ConfirmationDialog` too; it is a separate method and a separate\n  window.\n- A def with `targetWorldCell:false` passed a `tile` argument is REFUSED, not\n  silently coerced.\n- Nothing named by mod, def or comp: driven off `AbilityDef.targetWorldCell`.\n\n\n`ae84a07` is complete without this. The refusal is explicit, names the member,\nand says it is a capability gap rather than a game rule — the same disposition\n`attack`'s `queue-unsupported` takes (git-bug `bc2250b`).","files":null}]}